IF @mode != "publish"
    RETURN "Technical-summary publication was not selected."

IF @summary_exists != TRUE
    RETURN "Technical-summary publication requires an existing summary."

USE ../../references/technical-summary.md#summary-content AS summary_rules

DO Verify @request explicitly requests publication and @saved_summary has the
    matching @ticket_id with complete, placeholder-free content satisfying
    @summary_rules. Do not create or rewrite invalid content.

DO Resolve the private absolute acli and ix executables under shared Inux
    guidance. Report missing tools without setup, login, or version probes.
    Return an object with acli and ix. AS tools

RUN @tools.acli jira workitem comment list --key @ticket_id --json --paginate AS comments_result

DO Parse @comments_result.stdout as JSON. Check for duplicate summaries and
    material clarifications. Return an object with
    evidence_contradicts_summary, identical_comment, and duplicate_url. Never
    replace unrelated comments. AS comment_state

IF @comment_state.evidence_contradicts_summary == TRUE
    ASK "Jira evidence contradicts the saved summary. Type yes to revise it later, or no to leave it unchanged." AS revision_request

    DO Normalize @revision_request to lowercase "yes" or "no"; return "invalid"
        for every other answer. AS revision_choice

    IF @revision_choice == "yes"
        RETURN "Publication stopped. Run /inux ts improve with the new evidence; the saved summary is unchanged."

    IF @revision_choice == "no"
        RETURN "Publication stopped because evidence contradicts the draft; the saved summary is unchanged."

    RETURN "Publication stopped because the answer was not exactly yes or no; the saved summary is unchanged."

IF @comment_state.identical_comment == FALSE
    USE ../../references/cli.md AS cli_guidance

    DO Publish @saved_summary as one bounded transaction. Follow @cli_guidance.
        Create one unique private temporary directory and ADF path. Run @tools.ix
        with the separate arguments adf, @summary_path, and that path; verify the
        ADF faithfully represents @saved_summary. Immediately re-read the active
        ticket ID and saved summary, and do not publish if either differs from
        @ticket_id or @saved_summary. Then run @tools.acli with the separate
        arguments jira, workitem, comment, create, --key, @ticket_id, --body-file,
        the ADF path, and --json. Parse and verify the comment or ticket URL,
        looking it up only when absent. Remove only the unique temporary directory
        before completing or failing. Return the verified URL. AS publication_url
ELSE
    SET publication_url = @comment_state.duplicate_url

PRINT Report @publication_url or duplicate status briefly and leave task files unchanged.
